IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dda-rules`

-- Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (Cth) -- the questions of the person at work: the job seeker, employee, commission
-- agent, contract worker, partner, professional, union member or agency client who has a disability, or whose associate
-- has one, or who has a carer, assistant, assistance animal or disability aid.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Disability Discrimination Act 1992", Compilation No. 40
-- (1 July 2026), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts only. Judgments that belong to the Commission, a tribunal or a court (less favourable
-- treatment, reasonableness, unjustifiable hardship, inherent requirements) are asked as facts: "if it is accepted
-- that ...". Nothing here decides them.

§ `Disability Discrimination Act 1992 -- my questions at work`

§§ `Who and what the Act protects (ss 4, 7, 8, 9)`

@export Do I have a disability as the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (Cth) defines it (s 4)? A past, future (including a genetic predisposition) or imputed condition counts, and so does behaviour that is a symptom of it.
GIVEN `my condition` IS A `Kind of condition` @desc Which best describes your condition (now, in the past, in the future, or as others assume it to be)? Choose "none of these" if none fits.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I have a disability under the Act?` `my condition` MEANS
    `s 4 -- the condition is a disability` `my condition`

@export Is this person my "associate" under the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (s 4), so that I am protected from discrimination because of their disability (s 7)? Not answered where the Act's open list does not name the relationship.
GIVEN `who they are to me` IS A `Who the other person is to me` @desc Who is the person with the disability to you? A relative is related by blood, marriage, affinity or adoption.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is this person my associate under the Act?` `who they are to me` MEANS
    `s 4 -- the person is my associate` `who they are to me`

@export Does the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 count my carer, assistant, interpreter, reader, assistance animal or disability aid (s 9), so that I am protected from discrimination because I have it (s 8)?
GIVEN `what helps me` IS A `What assists me` @desc What is it: a carer, an assistant, an interpreter, a reader, another kind of helper, an animal, or equipment (including a palliative or therapeutic device)?
      `they help me because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person: do they give you assistance or services because of your disability?
      `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it accredited under a State or Territory law for animals trained to help a person with a disability?
      `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it accredited by an animal training organisation prescribed by the Disability Discrimination Regulations?
      `my animal is trained to help with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it trained to help you alleviate the effect of your disability?
      `my animal is trained to behave in public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it trained to meet standards of hygiene and behaviour appropriate for an animal in a public place?
      `I use the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For equipment: do you use it?
      `the equipment helps with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For equipment: does it help to alleviate the effect of your disability?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the Act count what helps me?` `what helps me` `they help me because of my disability` `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law` `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation` `my animal is trained to help with my disability` `my animal is trained to behave in public` `I use the equipment` `the equipment helps with my disability` MEANS
    `s 9 -- the Act counts what assists me`
        (`Section 9 facts` WITH
            `what it is` IS `what helps me`
            `helps because of the disability` IS `they help me because of my disability`
            `animal accredited under State or Territory law` IS `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law`
            `animal accredited by a prescribed organisation` IS `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation`
            `animal trained to alleviate the disability` IS `my animal is trained to help with my disability`
            `animal trained for public hygiene and behaviour` IS `my animal is trained to behave in public`
            `equipment used by me` IS `I use the equipment`
            `equipment alleviates the disability` IS `the equipment helps with my disability`)

§§ `Was it discrimination? (ss 5, 6, 10, 11)`

@export Did they discriminate against me as the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 defines it (ss 5, 6): less favourable treatment, a failure to make reasonable adjustments, or a requirement I cannot meet? Each judgment is asked as what a tribunal would accept.
GIVEN `I was treated less favourably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated (or are you to be treated) less favourably than a person without the disability would be in circumstances that are not materially different? Needing adjustments does not make the circumstances different (s 5(3)).
      `my disability was one of their reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disability one of the reasons, even if not the main one (s 10)?
      `they did not make adjustments for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they not make (or propose not to make) adjustments for you?
      `they have shown adjusting would be an unjustifiable hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they proved that making the adjustments would impose an unjustifiable hardship on them (s 11; the burden is theirs)?
      `not adjusting left me treated less favourably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did not making the adjustments have the effect that, because of the disability, you were treated less favourably than a person without it?
      `they required me to meet a requirement or condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they require you (or propose to require you) to comply with a requirement or condition?
      `I cannot meet it because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of the disability, do you not (or can you not) comply with it?
      `I could meet it only with adjustments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of the disability, could you comply with it only if they made adjustments for you?
      `it disadvantages people with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the requirement (or not adjusting) have, or is it likely to have, the effect of disadvantaging people with the disability?
      `they have shown the requirement is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they proved that the requirement or condition is reasonable in the circumstances (s 6(4); the burden is theirs)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Did they discriminate against me?` `I was treated less favourably` `my disability was one of their reasons` `they did not make adjustments for me` `they have shown adjusting would be an unjustifiable hardship` `not adjusting left me treated less favourably` `they required me to meet a requirement or condition` `I cannot meet it because of my disability` `I could meet it only with adjustments` `it disadvantages people with my disability` `they have shown the requirement is reasonable` MEANS
    JUST (`ss 5, 6 -- they discriminated` `the facts`)
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS
            `Discrimination facts` WITH
                `less favourable treatment` IS `I was treated less favourably`
                `disability one of the reasons` IS `my disability was one of their reasons`
                `adjustments not made` IS `they did not make adjustments for me`
                `hardship of adjusting shown` IS `they have shown adjusting would be an unjustifiable hardship`
                `not adjusting led to worse treatment` IS `not adjusting left me treated less favourably`
                `requirement imposed` IS `they required me to meet a requirement or condition`
                `cannot comply because of the disability` IS `I cannot meet it because of my disability`
                `could comply only with adjustments` IS `I could meet it only with adjustments`
                `disadvantages persons with the disability` IS `it disadvantages people with my disability`
                `requirement shown reasonable` IS `they have shown the requirement is reasonable`

§§ `Was it unlawful at work? (ss 12, 15-21B, 45-58)`

@export Which section of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 lists what was done to me, given my position at work (ss 15-21)? Not answered where no paragraph lists that act for that position.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `My position at work` @desc What is your position: job seeker, employee, commission agent (or seeking to be one), contract worker, partner (or invited to be one), holder of or applicant for a professional or trade authorisation, applicant or member of a registered union or employer organisation, or employment agency client?
      `what they did` IS A `What was done` @desc What did they do that you complain of?
      `number of partners` IS A NUMBER @desc For a partnership only: how many partners are there (or persons proposing to form it)? Enter 0 otherwise.
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Which section covers what was done to me at work?` `my position` `what they did` `number of partners` MEANS
    `ss 15-21 -- the paragraph that covers what was done` `my position` `what they did` `number of partners`

@export Does the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 reach what was done to me (s 12)? Its work provisions reach only the heads s 12 lists; registered organisations (s 20) are reached everywhere.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `My position at work` @desc What is your position at work?
      `it happened in a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in a Territory other than the ACT or the Northern Territory (for example Norfolk Island or Christmas Island)?
      `I am or seek to be a Commonwealth employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or are you seeking to become) a Commonwealth employee, such as an APS employee or a member of the Defence Force?
      `the qualification is under a Commonwealth law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a professional or trade authorisation: is it conferred under a Commonwealth law?
      `the Commonwealth did it using its powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done by the Commonwealth, a Territory Administration, or a Commonwealth or Territory statutory body, using a power given by a Commonwealth or Territory law?
      `a court accepts a treaty head` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been accepted that the provision, as applied to you, gives effect to ILO Convention 111, the ICCPR, the Disabilities Convention or the ICESCR, or relates to a matter external to Australia or of international concern (s 12(8))?
      `a corporation did it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done by a foreign corporation or an Australian trading or financial corporation (most companies), or by its officer or employee in the course of their duties?
      `it was in banking or insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in the course of banking or insurance business (other than State banking or insurance within one State)?
      `it was in interstate or overseas trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in the course of trade or commerce between Australia and overseas, among the States, or between a State and a Territory or two Territories?
      `it involved matters outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it involve persons, things or matters arising outside Australia?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the Act reach what was done to me?` `my position` `it happened in a Territory` `I am or seek to be a Commonwealth employee` `the qualification is under a Commonwealth law` `the Commonwealth did it using its powers` `a court accepts a treaty head` `a corporation did it` `it was in banking or insurance` `it was in interstate or overseas trade` `it involved matters outside Australia` MEANS
    JUST (`s 12 -- the Act reaches what was done` `my position` FALSE `the facts`)
    WHERE
        `the facts` MEANS
            `Reach facts` WITH
                `done in a Territory` IS `it happened in a Territory`
                `Commonwealth employment` IS `I am or seek to be a Commonwealth employee`
                `qualification under a Commonwealth law` IS `the qualification is under a Commonwealth law`
                `done by the Commonwealth using its powers` IS `the Commonwealth did it using its powers`
                `a treaty head accepted` IS `a court accepts a treaty head`
                `done by a foreign or trading or financial corporation` IS `a corporation did it`
                `in the business of banking or insurance` IS `it was in banking or insurance`
                `in interstate or overseas trade or commerce` IS `it was in interstate or overseas trade`
                `involving matters outside Australia` IS `it involved matters outside Australia`

@export Does the inherent requirements exception (s 21A) take what was done to me out of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992? It never applies to s 20 or to denied benefits or other detriment, except deciding who is offered promotion or transfer.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `My position at work` @desc What is your position at work?
      `what they did` IS A `What was done` @desc What did they do that you complain of?
      `it is about particular work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to particular work, including promotion or transfer to particular work?
      `I could not do the inherent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been accepted that, because of the disability, you would be unable to carry out the inherent requirements of that work even with reasonable adjustments (judged on your training, qualifications, experience and past performance, s 21A(2))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does the inherent requirements exception apply?` `my position` `what they did` `it is about particular work` `I could not do the inherent requirements` MEANS
    JUST (`s 21A -- the inherent requirements exception applies` `my position` `what they did` `it is about particular work` `I could not do the inherent requirements`)

@export Is what was done to me at work unlawful disability discrimination under the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (Part 2 Division 1)? The answer names the section that makes it unlawful, or why it is not, or that the Act does not answer.
GIVEN `my position` IS A `My position at work` @desc What is your position: job seeker, employee, commission agent (or seeking to be one), contract worker, partner (or invited to be one), holder of or applicant for a professional or trade authorisation, applicant or member of a registered union or employer organisation, or employment agency client?
      `what they did` IS A `What was done` @desc What did they do that you complain of?
      `number of partners` IS A NUMBER @desc For a partnership only: how many partners are there (or persons proposing to form it)? Enter 0 otherwise.
      `the job is domestic work in their home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a job you sought: is it to perform domestic duties on the premises where the employer lives?
      `the ground of it` IS A `The ground` @desc Was it because of your own disability, your carer, assistant, assistance animal or disability aid, or the disability of an associate of yours?
      `the condition` IS A `Kind of condition` @desc Which best describes the disability (yours, or your associate's), now, in the past, in the future or as assumed?
      `who the associate is` IS A `Who the other person is to me` @desc If it was an associate's disability: who are they to you? Otherwise choose "someone else".
      `what helps me` IS A `What assists me` @desc If it was your carer, assistant, animal or aid: what is it?
      `they help me because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person helping you: do they assist you because of your disability?
      `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it accredited under a State or Territory law for assistance animals?
      `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it accredited by a prescribed animal training organisation?
      `my animal is trained to help with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it trained to help you alleviate the effect of your disability?
      `my animal is trained to behave in public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it trained to meet standards of hygiene and behaviour for a public place?
      `I use the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For equipment: do you use it?
      `the equipment helps with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For equipment: does it help to alleviate the effect of your disability?
      `I was treated less favourably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated less favourably than a person without the disability would be in circumstances not materially different?
      `my disability was one of their reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the disability one of their reasons, even if not the main one?
      `they did not make adjustments for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they not make adjustments for you?
      `they have shown adjusting would be an unjustifiable hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they proved that making the adjustments would impose an unjustifiable hardship on them?
      `not adjusting left me treated less favourably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did not adjusting leave you, because of the disability, treated less favourably?
      `they required me to meet a requirement or condition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they require you to comply with a requirement or condition?
      `I cannot meet it because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of the disability, can you not comply with it?
      `I could meet it only with adjustments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could you comply with it only if they made adjustments?
      `it disadvantages people with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it (or not adjusting) disadvantage people with the disability?
      `they have shown the requirement is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they proved the requirement is reasonable in the circumstances?
      `it happened in a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in a Territory other than the ACT or the Northern Territory?
      `I am or seek to be a Commonwealth employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you (or are you seeking to become) a Commonwealth employee?
      `the qualification is under a Commonwealth law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a professional or trade authorisation: is it conferred under a Commonwealth law?
      `the Commonwealth did it using its powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth or Territory body using a Commonwealth or Territory power?
      `a court accepts a treaty head` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been accepted that the provision gives effect to a listed treaty or a matter of international concern (s 12(8))?
      `a corporation did it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done by a foreign, trading or financial corporation, or its officer or employee in the course of their duties?
      `it was in banking or insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in the course of banking or insurance business (not State business within one State)?
      `it was in interstate or overseas trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in the course of overseas or interstate trade or commerce?
      `it involved matters outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it involve persons, things or matters outside Australia?
      `it is about particular work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it relate to particular work, including promotion or transfer to it?
      `I could not do the inherent requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been accepted that you could not carry out the inherent requirements of that work even with reasonable adjustments?
      `they have shown avoiding it would be an unjustifiable hardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they proved that avoiding the discrimination would impose an unjustifiable hardship on them (s 21B)?
      `it was a special measure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it an act reasonably intended to give people with a disability equal opportunities, or to meet their special needs (s 45)?
      `the measure did not need to discriminate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was the discrimination not necessary for implementing the measure?
      `it is about my pay rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it about the rate of salary or wages paid to you?
      `it is about insurance or superannuation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it refusing to offer you, or the terms of, an annuity, an insurance policy, or membership of a superannuation or provident fund or scheme (s 46)?
      `it rests on reasonable actuarial data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was it based on actuarial or statistical data it was reasonable for them to rely on?
      `it is reasonable given the data` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: is it reasonable having regard to the data and other relevant factors?
      `no data could be had` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was no such data available and not reasonably obtainable?
      `it is reasonable given other factors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If no data could be had: is it reasonable having regard to other relevant factors?
      `they complied with a court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they act in direct compliance with an order of a court (s 47(1)(b))?
      `they complied with capacity-based wage rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they act in direct compliance with an industrial instrument or minimum-wage order setting wages by capacity for people who would otherwise get the disability support pension (s 47(1)(c), (d))?
      `they complied with a prescribed law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they act in direct compliance with a law prescribed by the regulations (s 47(2))?
      `my disability is infectious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disability an infectious disease?
      `it was needed to protect public health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was the discrimination reasonably necessary to protect public health (s 48)?
      `the Migration Act allowed it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it permitted or required by the Migration Act 1958 or an instrument under it (s 52)?
      `it is a Defence combat or peacekeeping role` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it about employment in the Defence Force in a combat, combat-related or peacekeeping position, prescribed circumstances, or as a chaplain or medical support person for such forces (s 53)?
      `it is selection for a peacekeeping force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it about selection for peacekeeping duties in a force raised for peacekeeping outside Australia (s 54)?
      `they suspected my animal was infectious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an assistance animal: did they reasonably suspect it has an infectious disease?
      `it was needed to protect health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was the discrimination reasonably necessary to protect public health or the health of other animals?
      `I did not produce evidence about my animal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an assistance animal: did they ask for evidence that it is an assistance animal or is trained for a public place, and you produced neither?
      `they had a Commission exemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they act in accordance with an exemption granted by the Australian Human Rights Commission (s 58)?
GIVETH A `What the Act says about what was done to me at work`
`Is what was done to me at work unlawful disability discrimination?` `my position` `what they did` `number of partners` `the job is domestic work in their home` `the ground of it` `the condition` `who the associate is` `what helps me` `they help me because of my disability` `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law` `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation` `my animal is trained to help with my disability` `my animal is trained to behave in public` `I use the equipment` `the equipment helps with my disability` `I was treated less favourably` `my disability was one of their reasons` `they did not make adjustments for me` `they have shown adjusting would be an unjustifiable hardship` `not adjusting left me treated less favourably` `they required me to meet a requirement or condition` `I cannot meet it because of my disability` `I could meet it only with adjustments` `it disadvantages people with my disability` `they have shown the requirement is reasonable` `it happened in a Territory` `I am or seek to be a Commonwealth employee` `the qualification is under a Commonwealth law` `the Commonwealth did it using its powers` `a court accepts a treaty head` `a corporation did it` `it was in banking or insurance` `it was in interstate or overseas trade` `it involved matters outside Australia` `it is about particular work` `I could not do the inherent requirements` `they have shown avoiding it would be an unjustifiable hardship` `it was a special measure` `the measure did not need to discriminate` `it is about my pay rate` `it is about insurance or superannuation` `it rests on reasonable actuarial data` `it is reasonable given the data` `no data could be had` `it is reasonable given other factors` `they complied with a court order` `they complied with capacity-based wage rules` `they complied with a prescribed law` `my disability is infectious` `it was needed to protect public health` `the Migration Act allowed it` `it is a Defence combat or peacekeeping role` `it is selection for a peacekeeping force` `they suspected my animal was infectious` `it was needed to protect health` `I did not produce evidence about my animal` `they had a Commission exemption` MEANS
    `Division 1 -- what the Act says` `my position` `what they did` `number of partners` `the job is domestic work in their home`
        `the ground of it` `the condition` `who the associate is` `the s 9 facts`
        `the discrimination facts` `the reach facts`
        `it is about particular work` `I could not do the inherent requirements` `they have shown avoiding it would be an unjustifiable hardship`
        `the exemption facts`
    WHERE
        `the s 9 facts` MEANS
            `Section 9 facts` WITH
                `what it is` IS `what helps me`
                `helps because of the disability` IS `they help me because of my disability`
                `animal accredited under State or Territory law` IS `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law`
                `animal accredited by a prescribed organisation` IS `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation`
                `animal trained to alleviate the disability` IS `my animal is trained to help with my disability`
                `animal trained for public hygiene and behaviour` IS `my animal is trained to behave in public`
                `equipment used by me` IS `I use the equipment`
                `equipment alleviates the disability` IS `the equipment helps with my disability`
        `the discrimination facts` MEANS
            `Discrimination facts` WITH
                `less favourable treatment` IS `I was treated less favourably`
                `disability one of the reasons` IS `my disability was one of their reasons`
                `adjustments not made` IS `they did not make adjustments for me`
                `hardship of adjusting shown` IS `they have shown adjusting would be an unjustifiable hardship`
                `not adjusting led to worse treatment` IS `not adjusting left me treated less favourably`
                `requirement imposed` IS `they required me to meet a requirement or condition`
                `cannot comply because of the disability` IS `I cannot meet it because of my disability`
                `could comply only with adjustments` IS `I could meet it only with adjustments`
                `disadvantages persons with the disability` IS `it disadvantages people with my disability`
                `requirement shown reasonable` IS `they have shown the requirement is reasonable`
        `the reach facts` MEANS
            `Reach facts` WITH
                `done in a Territory` IS `it happened in a Territory`
                `Commonwealth employment` IS `I am or seek to be a Commonwealth employee`
                `qualification under a Commonwealth law` IS `the qualification is under a Commonwealth law`
                `done by the Commonwealth using its powers` IS `the Commonwealth did it using its powers`
                `a treaty head accepted` IS `a court accepts a treaty head`
                `done by a foreign or trading or financial corporation` IS `a corporation did it`
                `in the business of banking or insurance` IS `it was in banking or insurance`
                `in interstate or overseas trade or commerce` IS `it was in interstate or overseas trade`
                `involving matters outside Australia` IS `it involved matters outside Australia`
        `the exemption facts` MEANS
            `Exemption facts` WITH
                `special measure` IS `it was a special measure`
                `discrimination not necessary for the measure` IS `the measure did not need to discriminate`
                `about rates of salary or wages` IS `it is about my pay rate`
                `about insurance or superannuation` IS `it is about insurance or superannuation`
                `based on reasonable actuarial or statistical data` IS `it rests on reasonable actuarial data`
                `reasonable given the data and other factors` IS `it is reasonable given the data`
                `no data available or obtainable` IS `no data could be had`
                `reasonable given other factors` IS `it is reasonable given other factors`
                `complying with a court order` IS `they complied with a court order`
                `complying with capacity-based wage provisions` IS `they complied with capacity-based wage rules`
                `complying with a prescribed law` IS `they complied with a prescribed law`
                `the disability is an infectious disease` IS `my disability is infectious`
                `necessary to protect public health` IS `it was needed to protect public health`
                `Migration Act permits or requires it` IS `the Migration Act allowed it`
                `Defence Force combat or peacekeeping position` IS `it is a Defence combat or peacekeeping role`
                `selection for a peacekeeping force` IS `it is selection for a peacekeeping force`
                `animal suspected of infectious disease` IS `they suspected my animal was infectious`
                `necessary to protect health of people or animals` IS `it was needed to protect health`
                `animal evidence asked for and not produced` IS `I did not produce evidence about my animal`
                `acting under a Commission exemption` IS `they had a Commission exemption`

@export Is what was done to me at work unlawful under the Disability Discrimination Act 1992, as yes, no or not answered? Yes: unlawful. No: outside the Act's reach, or an exception or exemption applies. Not answered: not discrimination, not a covered ground, or an act the work provisions do not list.
GIVEN `what the Act says` IS A `What the Act says about what was done to me at work` @desc The answer to "Is what was done to me at work unlawful disability discrimination?".
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it unlawful, yes or no?` `what the Act says` MEANS
    `Division 1 -- unlawful` `what the Act says`

§§ `Harassment at work (s 35) -- if I was harassed`

@export Is the harassment I suffered at work unlawful under s 35 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992? It covers harassment by my employer, a co-worker, a prospective employer, or a principal or fellow agent or contract worker; not by a customer or stranger.
GIVEN `who harassed me` IS A `Who harassed me` @desc Who harassed you?
      `it was about the disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you harassed in relation to the disability ("harass" is not defined in the Act; a tribunal decides)?
      `the ground of it` IS A `The ground` @desc Is the disability yours, or your carer's, assistant's, animal's or aid's, or an associate's?
      `the condition` IS A `Kind of condition` @desc Which best describes the disability?
      `who the associate is` IS A `Who the other person is to me` @desc If it was an associate's disability: who are they to you? Otherwise choose "someone else".
      `what helps me` IS A `What assists me` @desc If it was your carer, assistant, animal or aid: what is it?
      `they help me because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a person helping you: do they assist you because of your disability?
      `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it accredited under a State or Territory law?
      `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it accredited by a prescribed training organisation?
      `my animal is trained to help with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it trained to help with your disability?
      `my animal is trained to behave in public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an animal: is it trained for hygiene and behaviour in a public place?
      `I use the equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For equipment: do you use it?
      `the equipment helps with my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For equipment: does it help to alleviate the effect of your disability?
      `it happened in a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done in a Territory other than the ACT or the Northern Territory?
      `the Commonwealth did it using its powers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth or Territory body using a Commonwealth or Territory power?
      `a court accepts a treaty head` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been accepted that s 35 as applied gives effect to a listed treaty or a matter of international concern (s 12(8))?
      `a corporation did it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it done by a foreign, trading or financial corporation, or its officer or employee in the course of their duties?
      `it was in banking or insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in the course of banking or insurance business?
      `it was in interstate or overseas trade` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it in the course of overseas or interstate trade or commerce?
      `it involved matters outside Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it involve persons, things or matters outside Australia?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the harassment unlawful?` `who harassed me` `it was about the disability` `the ground of it` `the condition` `who the associate is` `what helps me` `they help me because of my disability` `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law` `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation` `my animal is trained to help with my disability` `my animal is trained to behave in public` `I use the equipment` `the equipment helps with my disability` `it happened in a Territory` `the Commonwealth did it using its powers` `a court accepts a treaty head` `a corporation did it` `it was in banking or insurance` `it was in interstate or overseas trade` `it involved matters outside Australia` MEANS
    `s 35 -- the harassment is unlawful` `who harassed me` `it was about the disability`
        `the ground of it` `the condition` `who the associate is`
        (`Section 9 facts` WITH
            `what it is` IS `what helps me`
            `helps because of the disability` IS `they help me because of my disability`
            `animal accredited under State or Territory law` IS `my animal is accredited under a State or Territory law`
            `animal accredited by a prescribed organisation` IS `my animal is accredited by a prescribed training organisation`
            `animal trained to alleviate the disability` IS `my animal is trained to help with my disability`
            `animal trained for public hygiene and behaviour` IS `my animal is trained to behave in public`
            `equipment used by me` IS `I use the equipment`
            `equipment alleviates the disability` IS `the equipment helps with my disability`)
        (`Reach facts` WITH
            `done in a Territory` IS `it happened in a Territory`
            -- s 12(5), (6) do not reach Division 3; these two fields are read only for ss 15-17 and 19.
            `Commonwealth employment` IS FALSE
            `qualification under a Commonwealth law` IS FALSE
            `done by the Commonwealth using its powers` IS `the Commonwealth did it using its powers`
            `a treaty head accepted` IS `a court accepts a treaty head`
            `done by a foreign or trading or financial corporation` IS `a corporation did it`
            `in the business of banking or insurance` IS `it was in banking or insurance`
            `in interstate or overseas trade or commerce` IS `it was in interstate or overseas trade`
            `involving matters outside Australia` IS `it involved matters outside Australia`)

§§ `Victimisation (ss 42, 58A) -- if I was punished for complaining`

@export Was I victimised under the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 (s 58A): subjected or threatened with a detriment because I complained, took proceedings, gave information, attended a conference, was a witness, asserted rights, or made an allegation, or because they believed I did? Victimisation is unlawful everywhere in Australia.
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc What did you do, or propose to do? Choose "none of these" if none.
      `they believed I did one of these` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they believe you had done, or proposed to do, one of these things?
      `they subjected or threatened me with a detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they subject you, or threaten to subject you, to any detriment?
      `that was why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it on the ground of what you did, or what they believed you did?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Was I victimised?` `what I did` `they believed I did one of these` `they subjected or threatened me with a detriment` `that was why` MEANS
    JUST (NOT (`s 58A(1) -- the prohibition was kept` (`s 58A(2) -- an act of victimisation` `what I did` `they believed I did one of these` `they subjected or threatened me with a detriment` `that was why`)))

@export What is the most imprisonment, in months, the person who victimised me faces for the offence in s 42 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992? 0 if there was no victimisation, or if they are an individual liable only through their employee's or agent's conduct (s 123(5)).
GIVEN `what I did` IS A `What I did` @desc What did you do, or propose to do? Choose "none of these" if none.
      `they believed I did one of these` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they believe you had done, or proposed to do, one of these things?
      `they subjected or threatened me with a detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they subject you, or threaten to subject you, to any detriment?
      `that was why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it on the ground of what you did, or what they believed you did?
      `they are liable only through someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you ask about an individual (not a company) who would be convicted only because of what their employee or agent did (s 123(3), (4))?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`The most imprisonment for victimising me` `what I did` `they believed I did one of these` `they subjected or threatened me with a detriment` `that was why` `they are liable only through someone else` MEANS
    `s 42 -- the most months of imprisonment`
        (`s 58A(2) -- an act of victimisation` `what I did` `they believed I did one of these` `they subjected or threatened me with a detriment` `that was why`)
        `they are liable only through someone else`

§§ `Who else answers for it (ss 122, 123)`

@export Is my employer (or other principal) taken to have done what its director, employee or agent did to me (s 123 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992)? Yes unless the employer proves it took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence.
GIVEN `they acted within their authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the director, employee or agent act on the employer's behalf within the scope of their actual or apparent authority?
      `the employer proved precautions and diligence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the employer proved it took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my employer answerable for what its people did?` `they acted within their authority` `the employer proved precautions and diligence` MEANS
    `s 123 -- the employer is taken to have done it` `they acted within their authority` `the employer proved precautions and diligence`

@export Is a person who caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted the unlawful act against me taken also to have done it (s 122 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992)?
GIVEN `they caused or instructed or helped or permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did this person cause, instruct, induce, aid or permit another person to do the act?
      `the act was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act unlawful under Division 1, 2, 2A, 3 or 6 of Part 2 (discrimination, disability standards, harassment or victimisation)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the person who caused it also answerable?` `they caused or instructed or helped or permitted it` `the act was unlawful` MEANS
    `s 122 -- they are taken to have done the act` `they caused or instructed or helped or permitted it` `the act was unlawful`

§§ `Job advertisements (s 44) -- if I saw one`

@export Was the job advertisement or notice I saw an offence under s 44 of the Disability Discrimination Act 1992, and what is the most penalty, in penalty units? Not answered where s 44 does not apply.
GIVEN `they published it or let it be published` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person publish or display the advertisement or notice, or cause or permit it to be?
      `it shows an intention to discriminate unlawfully` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate, or could it reasonably be understood as indicating, an intention to do an act made unlawful by the Act (such as refusing to employ people with a disability)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is the most penalty for the advertisement?` `they published it or let it be published` `it shows an intention to discriminate unlawfully` MEANS
    `s 44 -- the most penalty units for the advertisement` `they published it or let it be published` `it shows an intention to discriminate unlawfully`

§§ `Where I complain (s 13(4)) -- if I have already gone to a State or Territory body`

@export Am I barred from complaining to the Australian Human Rights Commission under the Disability Discrimination Act 1992 because I already complained or sued under a State or Territory discrimination law about the same act (s 13(4))?
GIVEN `the State law covers the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the State or Territory discrimination law deal with the matter the complaint is about?
      `I already complained or sued under it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made a complaint or started a proceeding under that State or Territory law about the same act or omission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I barred from complaining under this Act?` `the State law covers the matter` `I already complained or sued under it` MEANS
    JUST (`s 13(4) -- I am barred from a complaint under this Act` `the State law covers the matter` `I already complained or sued under it`)
